    'body' => <<<'HTML'
<p>Insurance claims are supposed to bring relief after property damage. In practice, they often bring delays, confusing letters, and estimates that do not match what the repairs actually cost. Port Arthur Public Adjuster exists to give homeowners and business owners in Port Arthur, Jefferson County, and the surrounding Golden Triangle someone in their corner during that process: a licensed public adjuster who works for the policyholder, not the insurance company.</p>
<p>Your insurer has its own adjusters, estimators, and claim reviewers. We believe you deserve informed representation, too.</p>

<h2>Who operates Port Arthur Public Adjuster</h2>
<p>Port Arthur Public Adjuster is a public adjusting service of <strong>[[company]]</strong>, licensed by the Texas Department of Insurance (TDI license #[[license]]). We serve Port Arthur, Jefferson County, and surrounding Southeast Texas communities, and we meet clients at their damaged property rather than at a storefront office.</p>
<p>Claims are led by <a href="/author/joseph-dittman/">Joseph Dittman</a>, a licensed Texas public adjuster, certified insurance appraiser, insurance umpire, and expert witness. His background includes carrier-side adjusting, public adjusting, appraisal work, expert witness support, and hands-on construction experience, across residential, commercial, storm, hail, wind, water, fire, hurricane, and catastrophe losses. He also reviews the articles published on this site.</p>

<h2>Who we serve</h2>
<p>No two Port Arthur claims are the same. A hurricane that tears shingles off a pier-and-beam home in one neighborhood, a tropical downpour that sends water into a slab home in another, a kitchen fire, or a burst pipe during a hard freeze all raise different questions. We work with:</p>
